<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The small icon of every MilO notification: the app's mark, a rounded square with the "M" cut
    out of it (Shawn's choice of 2026-10-07). Android draws it itself, in the status bar and the
    notification shade, using only the shape: every opaque pixel is painted in one colour of the
    system's choosing, so the lime of the mark cannot be in here. The lime is the notifications'
    colour instead (res/values/colors.xml), which Android uses around this shape where it adds
    colour at all. That is why the size and the white fill are written here and not taken from
    the design tokens, which exist only inside Compose.

    The square is 20 of the 24 units wide, the margin Android's status bar icons keep, with the
    mark's corner (11 on 36, so 6 here). The letter is the launcher icon's "M"
    (ic_launcher_foreground.xml, read from res/font/sora.ttf at weight 700), halved and moved to
    the middle. It is larger on the square than on the mark, 12 of 20 units wide instead of a
    third: at the mark's size its strokes would be about one pixel wide in the status bar.

    One path: the square and the letter are both in it, and "evenOdd" makes the letter a hole.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M8,2h8a6,6 0,0 1,6 6v8a6,6 0,0 1,-6 6h-8a6,6 0,0 1,-6 -6v-8a6,6 0,0 1,6 -6z M5.945,17.475L5.945,6.525L9.335,6.525L11.835,12.685L12.12,12.685L14.6,6.525L18.055,6.525L18.055,17.475L15.615,17.475L15.615,8.13L15.97,8.16L13.075,15.255L10.725,15.255L7.82,8.16L8.2,8.13L8.2,17.475z" />
</vector>
